---
description: ER Explorer monorepo conventions for agents and contributors
alwaysApply: true
---

You are working on ER Explorer.

Always:
- read the docs before editing code (`docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/REPRODUCIBILITY.md`)
- keep wide datasets canonical
- derive long analysis views lazily (`@er-explorer/data`)
- keep analysis separate from rendering (`@er-explorer/analysis` / plugins vs `@er-explorer/renderer`)
- preserve reproducibility (session files, checksums, bootstrap seeds)
- prefer small, mergeable changes
- add tests and docs with meaningful changes

Never:
- collapse everything into a single React file
- mix rendering and statistical logic inside renderer layers
- force the user to manage wide/long conversions manually
- break session reproducibility
- resurrect deleted `packages/visualization-engine`
